 have our own notes: A strengths, concerns; B strengths, concerns; C strengths, concerns; D strengths, concerns. We need to evaluate.\n\nWe have evidence: A anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership. Concerns: show-off, not open to new ideas, unfriendly, eats unhealthily. No direct evidence on stress resilience, decision quality, attention accuracy, adaptability.\n\nB: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone, makes nasty remarks, grumpy, uncooperative, weak memory for numbers.\n\nC: makes correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, moody, loner, hot temper.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best fits overall. Let's weigh.\n\nOperational reliability: B very conscientious, D takes responsibility seriously, A leadership, C puts concern for others.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well, C keeps calm in crisis, D responds adequately, A unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision; B computer skills, weather assessment; C understands complicated technology; D solves problems extremely well.\n\nDecision quality: C makes correct decisions quickly, A anticipates dangerous situations, D responds adequately.\n\nCrew cooperation: A show-off, not open to ideas, unfriendly; B nasty remarks, uncooperative; C egocentric, difficulty communicating; D moody, loner, hot temper.\n\nAll have cooperation concerns. Which is least severe? Hard to gauge. Show-off may be less severe than nasty remarks. Egocentric and communication difficulty may be severe. Hot temper may be severe. So perhaps A is still best.\n\nBut we lack stress resilience evidence for A. However B's stress resilience is proven. But B's crew cooperation issues are severe. The panel seems leaning to A now. As Agent 3, we can update our vote to A, acknowledging the arguments.\n\nWe should also bring up that Candidate C has strong decision-making and calmness, but communication issues are concerning. Could be a tie-breaker? But we can note that C's egocentric attitude and lack of willingness to further education may hinder long-term development.\n\nWe need to make a focused argumentative contribution: state current recommendation (maybe Candidate A), reference discussion (agents 1 and 2 reaffirmed A, Agent 3 earlier leaned B), provide evidence (A's anticipation, leadership, spatial vision vs B's stress handling but crew issues), and explain why A still best.\n\nThus we will vote Candidate A.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate A\"."}
